Title: A Chaotic Orbit as a Magnifying Glass.
Note: x becomes x times x minus 2 (the Chebyshev map, conjugate to the logistic map at r = 4), which doubles a small error at each step.
Note: A one-ulp difference in any single operation of any backend reaches the whole value within about 60 steps, so the printed bits fingerprint every rounding of the run. Prior art: Rosinski and Williamson 1997 used chaotic sensitivity to validate climate-model ports.
§1 Decimals are floats.
§2 Let x be 0.1234567.
§3 For each n from 1 to 3000, do the following.
§3.1 Set x to x times x minus 2.0.
§3.2 If the remainder of n by 500 is zero, say "step " followed by n followed by ": " followed by x.
§4 It must hold that x is at least -2.0 and x is at most 2.0.
